# =====================================================================================================================
# Akeeba Release System — JSON:API request collection
# =====================================================================================================================
#
# This file documents every JSON:API endpoint ARS exposes. It is a PHPStorm / IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client file: open it
# in the IDE and click the ▶ gutter icon next to a request to run it.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SETUP
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. On the target site enable the "Web Services - Akeeba Release System" plugin. Without it none of the `v1/ars/…`
#    routes exist and every request below returns a 404.
# 2. Enable the "API Authentication - Joomla Token" plugin and the "User - Joomla API Token" plugin, then generate a
#    token for the user you want to act as (User Profile → Joomla API Token).
# 3. Copy `http-client.private.env.json-dist` to `http-client.private.env.json` (it is git-ignored) and put the token
#    in it. Set the site URL in `http-client.env.json`. Both files live next to this one.
# 4. Pick the `dev` environment in the HTTP Client's environment selector before running anything.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AUTHENTICATION AND AUTHORISATION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Every request must be authenticated. The token identifies a Joomla user and that user's permissions are enforced —
# an API token is NOT a bypass. Being a Super User is not assumed anywhere.
#
#   * Reading anything other than your own Download IDs requires `core.manage` on `com_ars`, i.e. the same privilege
#     that lets you open the component in the back-end. Without it you get 403, not a filtered list.
#   * Creating a release, item, update stream or automatic item description requires `core.create` on the ARS category
#     it belongs to (`com_ars.category.<id>`). Editing requires `core.edit` on that category, deleting `core.delete`.
#   * Categories are their own asset: creating one requires `core.create` on `com_ars`, editing and deleting require
#     the privilege on `com_ars.category.<id>`.
#   * Environments are component-wide, so their write operations are authorised against `com_ars` itself.
#   * Download ID labels are special, see the Download ID labels section below.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONVENTIONS USED BY EVERY LIST ENDPOINT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   Pagination      `page[limit]=50&page[offset]=100`. The default page size is 20.
#   Sorting         `list_ordering=<column>&list_direction=asc|desc`. A column the model does not know is ignored
#                   rather than rejected. The valid columns are listed with each endpoint.
#   Search          `search=<needle>` is the same free-text box as the back-end. On most endpoints `search=id:123`
#                   switches it to an exact ID lookup.
#   Empty filters   A filter you do not send is not applied. Sending an empty string is the same as not sending it.
#
# Responses are JSON:API documents: the records are under `data`, each with `id`, `type` and `attributes`.
#
# =====================================================================================================================


# =====================================================================================================================
# CATEGORIES — /v1/ars/categories
# =====================================================================================================================
#
# Filters: search, published, show_unauth_links, supported, access, language
# Sort by: id, title, type, created, access, show_unauth_links, published, is_supported, language, ordering

### Categories: raw list
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/categories
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Categories: search by title, only published, newest first
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/categories?search=Data+Compliance&published=1&list_ordering=id&list_direction=desc
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Categories: second page of 50, only the ones flagged as supported
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/categories?supported=1&page[limit]=50&page[offset]=50
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Categories: fetch one
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/categories/1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0


# =====================================================================================================================
# RELEASES — /v1/ars/releases
# =====================================================================================================================
#
# Filters: search, category_id, published, maturity, minMaturity, show_unauth_links, access (single value or repeated
#          as access[]=…), language, latest
# Sort by: r.id, r.version, r.category_id, maturity, r.created, r.access, show_unauth_links, published, r.language,
#          r.ordering (the unprefixed forms — id, version, category_id, created, access, language, ordering — work too)

### Releases: raw list
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/releases
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Releases: one category, stable or better, most recent first
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/releases?category_id=1&minMaturity=stable&list_ordering=id&list_direction=desc
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Releases: find an exact version number
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/releases?category_id=1&search=version%3A1.0.0
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Releases: only the latest release of each category
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/releases?latest=1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Releases: fetch one
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/releases/81
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Releases: create one
POST {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/releases
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "category_id": 1,
  "version": "3.0.0",
  "alias": "3-0-0",
  "maturity": "stable",
  "notes": "<p>Release notes go here.</p>",
  "access": 1,
  "published": 1,
  "language": "*"
}

### Releases: update one
# PATCH merges: any column you leave out keeps its current value.
PATCH {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/releases/81
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "maturity": "stable",
  "notes": "Once upon a time, in a galaxy far, far away someone created a random UUID4: {{$uuid}}",
  "published": 1
}

### Releases: delete one
DELETE {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/releases/81
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0


# =====================================================================================================================
# ITEMS (files and links) — /v1/ars/items
# =====================================================================================================================
#
# Filters: search, category_id, release_id, published, show_unauth_links, access, language
# Sort by: i.id, i.release_id, i.title, i.created, i.access, i.show_unauth_links, i.published, i.language, i.ordering,
#          c.id (the unprefixed forms work too, but prefer the prefixed ones: the query joins three tables)
#
# The `environments` attribute is the raw stored value on list responses and a decoded array on single-item responses.
#
# DELETE accepts two extra query parameters: `delete_file=1` also removes the file from the repository directory, and
# `delete_empty_directory=1` additionally removes the directory if that left it empty.

### Items: raw list
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/items
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Items: everything in one release
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/items?release_id=81
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Items: find the item serving a specific URL
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/items?release_id=81&search=link:https://d16g1oj796wk12.cloudfront.net/downloads/test_package/2.0.0/pkg_test-core.zip
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Items: fetch one
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/items/161
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Items: delete one, together with its file and the directory it left empty
DELETE {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/items/161?delete_file=1&delete_empty_directory=1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0


# =====================================================================================================================
# AUTOMATIC ITEM DESCRIPTIONS — /v1/ars/autodescriptions
# =====================================================================================================================
#
# These are the templates ARS applies to a newly created item whose filename matches `packname`: they supply the item's
# title, description, access level and — the interesting part — its list of environments.
#
# Filters: search (title, description, packname; `id:N` for an exact ID), id, category_id, title, packname,
#          environment_id, created_by, show_unauth_links, access (single value or repeated as access[]=…), published
# Sort by: a.id, a.title, a.category, a.packname, a.access, a.created, a.created_by, a.modified, a.published,
#          cat_title, cat_alias, cat_type
#
# NOTE ON `category`: the column is called `category`, not `category_id` — but the LIST FILTER is `category_id`, to
# match the other endpoints. When you POST or PATCH, send `category`.
#
# NOTE ON `environments`: on list responses this is a decoded array of environment IDs. On single-item responses it is
# whatever the table object holds, which is an array of ID strings. Treat both as "cast each element to int".

### Autodescriptions: raw list
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/autodescriptions
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Autodescriptions: everything defined for one category
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/autodescriptions?category_id=1&published=1&list_ordering=a.packname&list_direction=asc
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Autodescriptions: the ones matching a particular package name pattern
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/autodescriptions?packname=pkg_ars
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Autodescriptions: every record which still lists environment #7
# Use this before you retire or renumber an environment.
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/autodescriptions?environment_id=7
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Autodescriptions: fetch one
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/autodescriptions/1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Autodescriptions: create one
POST {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/autodescriptions
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "category": 1,
  "packname": "pkg_ars-*-core.zip",
  "title": "Akeeba Release System (core)",
  "description": "<p>The free of charge version.</p>",
  "environments": ["3", "7"],
  "access": 1,
  "published": 1
}

### Autodescriptions: replace the environments of one record
# This is the write half of use case 1: point the automatic description at the environments you actually support.
PATCH {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/autodescriptions/1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "environments": ["3", "7", "11"]
}

### Autodescriptions: delete one
DELETE {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/autodescriptions/1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0


# =====================================================================================================================
# ENVIRONMENTS — /v1/ars/environments
# =====================================================================================================================
#
# An environment is a `platform/version` pair, e.g. `php/8.3` or `joomla/5.2`. `title` is the human readable label
# shown in the back-end; `xmltitle` is the machine readable value which ends up in the update XML.
#
# Filters: search (title and xmltitle; `id:N` for an exact ID), id, title, xmltitle, platform, created_by
# Sort by: id, title, xmltitle, created, created_by, modified, modified_by
#
# `platform` is anchored: `platform=php` matches `php/8.3` but not `myphp/1.0`. `xmltitle` is a partial match, so
# `xmltitle=8.3` finds `php/8.3` regardless of platform.

### Environments: raw list
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/environments
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Environments: every PHP version, sorted by XML title
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/environments?platform=php&list_ordering=xmltitle&list_direction=asc&page[limit]=100
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Environments: does an environment for this exact version already exist?
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/environments?xmltitle=php/8.5
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Environments: fetch one
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/environments/7
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Environments: create one
# The XML title must be `platform/version`. The version part must be numeric and dot separated; only the `wordpress`
# platform additionally accepts a trailing `+`.
POST {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/environments
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "PHP 8.5",
  "xmltitle": "php/8.5"
}

### Environments: rename one
PATCH {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/environments/7
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "PHP 8.5 (current)"
}

### Environments: delete one
DELETE {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/environments/7
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0


# =====================================================================================================================
# UPDATE STREAMS — /v1/ars/updatestreams
# =====================================================================================================================
#
# An update stream is what Joomla's extension updater talks to. Its URLs are predictable and built from the stream's
# numeric id (the alias is only a URL-safe label; it does not appear in these URLs):
#
#   XML update source   {{host}}/index.php?option=com_ars&view=update&task=stream&format=xml&id=<id>
#   JSON update source  {{host}}/index.php?option=com_ars&view=update&task=stream&format=json&id=<id>
#   Download redirect   {{host}}/index.php?option=com_ars&view=update&task=download&format=raw&id=<id>
#   Whole category      {{host}}/index.php?option=com_ars&view=update&task=category&format=xml&id=<category id>
#
# Append `&dlid=<download id>` to fetch them as a subscriber would. So once you know the stream's id you can fetch the
# exact XML Joomla is being served.
#
# Filters: search (name, alias, element; `id:N` for an exact ID), id, category_id, name, alias (exact), type, element
#          (exact), folder (exact), packname, client_id, created_by, published
# Sort by: a.id, a.name, a.alias, a.type, a.element, a.category, a.packname, a.client_id, a.folder, a.created,
#          a.created_by, a.modified, a.published, cat_title, cat_alias, cat_type
#
# NOTE ON `category`: as with the automatic item descriptions, the LIST FILTER is `category_id` but the column you
# POST or PATCH is `category`.

### Update streams: raw list
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/updatestreams
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Update streams: everything defined for one category
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/updatestreams?category_id=1&published=1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Update streams: the stream serving a specific Joomla extension
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/updatestreams?type=packages&element=pkg_ars
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Update streams: look one up by its alias
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/updatestreams?alias=akeeba-release-system
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Update streams: every back-end plugin stream
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/updatestreams?type=plugins&folder=system&client_id=0
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Update streams: fetch one
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/updatestreams/3
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Update streams: fetch the XML that stream actually serves
# Not a JSON:API endpoint — this is the public update source URL, requested exactly the way Joomla requests it.
GET {{host}}/index.php?option=com_ars&view=update&task=stream&format=xml&id=3
Accept: application/xml
User-Agent: Joomla/5.0

### Update streams: create one
POST {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/updatestreams
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Akeeba Release System",
  "alias": "akeeba-release-system",
  "type": "packages",
  "element": "pkg_ars",
  "category": 1,
  "packname": "pkg_ars-*.zip",
  "client_id": 0,
  "folder": "",
  "published": 1
}

### Update streams: update one
PATCH {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/updatestreams/3
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "published": 1,
  "packname": "pkg_ars-*.zip"
}

### Update streams: delete one
DELETE {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/updatestreams/3
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0


# =====================================================================================================================
# DOWNLOAD ID LABELS — /v1/ars/dlidlabels
# =====================================================================================================================
#
# A Download ID is a bearer credential: whoever knows the string can download everything its owner is subscribed to.
# The endpoint is therefore authorised differently from the rest:
#
#   * Any authenticated user may list and read THEIR OWN records. The `user_id` filter is silently forced to their own
#     ID, so there is no way to page into somebody else's.
#   * Seeing other people's records requires `core.manage` on `com_ars`, i.e. back-end access to the component.
#   * Creating a record for another user, and editing anybody else's record, requires `core.admin` on `com_ars`.
#   * Nobody — not even the owner — may edit the primary ("main") Download ID through the API. Its title is fixed and
#     it can never be unpublished.
#   * Deleting your own record is always allowed; deleting somebody else's needs `core.delete` on `com_ars`.
#
# Filters: search (user name and username; `id:N` for an exact ID), id, user_id, dlid (partial, and it understands the
#          `<user_id>:<dlid>` form), title, username (exact), name (partial), email (exact), primary, published
# Sort by: i.id, i.title, i.user_id, i.dlid, i.primary, i.created, i.published, u.name, u.username, u.email
#
# The `name`, `username` and `email` attributes come from a join against `#__users` and are only present on LIST
# responses. Fetching a single record returns the Download ID label columns alone.

### Download ID labels: raw list
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Download ID labels: everything belonging to one user, published and unpublished
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels?user_id=70&list_ordering=i.primary&list_direction=desc
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Download ID labels: only the disabled ones of that user
# This is what tells you why their update is failing: an unpublished Download ID is refused.
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels?user_id=70&published=0
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Download ID labels: who owns this Download ID?
# The response carries user_id, name, username and email — the whole of use case 2 in one request.
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels?dlid=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Download ID labels: the same, for a Download ID in `<user_id>:<dlid>` form
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels?dlid=70%3A0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Download ID labels: find a user's records by their email address
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels?email=someone%40example.com
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Download ID labels: find a user's records by username
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels?username=someone
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Download ID labels: only the primary Download IDs
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels?primary=1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Download ID labels: fetch one
GET {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels/12
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0

### Download ID labels: create an additional Download ID
# Omit `dlid` and ARS generates a unique one for you. Omit `user_id` and it belongs to the token's own user;
# supplying somebody else's user_id requires core.admin.
POST {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": 70,
  "title": "CI server",
  "published": 1
}

### Download ID labels: disable one
PATCH {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels/12
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "published": 0
}

### Download ID labels: rotate one
# Sending an empty `dlid` makes ARS generate a fresh, non-colliding Download ID. Do NOT send null — nulls are ignored.
PATCH {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels/12
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dlid": ""
}

### Download ID labels: delete one
DELETE {{host}}/api/index.php/v1/ars/dlidlabels/12
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
X-Joomla-Token: {{token}}
User-Agent: AkeebaReleaseMaker/2.0


# =====================================================================================================================
# RECIPES
# =====================================================================================================================
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Which PHP and Joomla versions will the next release in category N be marked as supporting?
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   a. GET /v1/ars/autodescriptions?category_id=N&published=1
#      Every automatic item description that will be applied to the files of the next release.
#   b. Collect the `environments` arrays from those records and take their union.
#   c. GET /v1/ars/environments?page[limit]=100
#      Read the whole environment vocabulary once and index it by id; `xmltitle` gives you `php/8.3`, `joomla/5.2`.
#   d. Compare that against the `require` / `extra` compatibility declarations in your composer.json.
#   e. For anything missing: POST /v1/ars/environments to create it, then
#      PATCH /v1/ars/autodescriptions/<id> with the corrected `environments` array.
#
#   Before deleting an environment that turned out to be obsolete, check nothing still points at it:
#   GET /v1/ars/autodescriptions?environment_id=<id>
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. A subscriber's update is failing. Who are they and what Download IDs do they have?
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   From a Download ID string:
#     GET /v1/ars/dlidlabels?dlid=<the string>      → user_id, name, username, email
#   From a user:
#     GET /v1/ars/dlidlabels?user_id=<id>           → all their records, published and unpublished
#     GET /v1/ars/dlidlabels?email=<address>        → the same, if all you have is an email address
#
#   An unpublished record, or a Download ID which matches no record at all, is the usual answer.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. The update XML looks wrong. Which stream produced it?
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   a. GET /v1/ars/categories?search=<software name>          → the category id
#   b. GET /v1/ars/updatestreams?category_id=<id>             → the stream, its alias, type, element and packname
#   c. GET /index.php?option=com_ars&view=update&task=stream&format=xml&id=<stream id>
#      The XML Joomla is actually being served. Add `&dlid=<download id>` to see a subscriber's view of it.
#   d. GET /v1/ars/releases?category_id=<id>&published=1      → the releases that should be in it
#      GET /v1/ars/items?release_id=<id>                      → the files, and whether their names match `packname`
#
#   A file which does not match the stream's `packname` pattern is silently absent from the XML; that is by far the
#   most common cause of a discrepancy.
